  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pg (Sk. Moniruddin vs The State Of West Bengal & on 13 August, 2015 Author: Dipankar Datta",
    "facts": "The respondents 7 and 8, it has been alleged in the writ petition, are carrying on hotel (dhaba) business without obtaining necessary licences from the relevant authorities. Since the respondents 7 and 8 are unrepresented despite service, it has not been possible for this Bench to ascertain as to whether they have obtained the necessary licences or not.",
    "arguments": "Learned advocates representing the petitioner and the official respondents are ad idem that licences are required to be obtained under Section 201 of the West Bengal Municipal Act, 1993 as well as under the Fire Prevention and Fire Safety Rules, 2003 and the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned advocates representing the petitioner and the official respondents are ad idem that licences are required to be obtained under Section 201 of the West Bengal Municipal Act, 1993 as well as under the Fire Prevention and Fire Safety Rules, 2003 and the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
